      "items": [
        "Competitive exams frequently ask about local terminology: Reg deserts are called 'Serir' in Libya and Algeria.",
        "Wind deflation is the key process forming Reg deserts by selectively blowing away finer sand particles.",
        "Hamada deserts consist of massive exposed bedrock, smoothed and scoured by wind abrasion."
      ],
      "id": "tcewp2c"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Erg deserts are vast stretches of undulating sand dunes shaped primarily by wind deposition.",
        "Reg or Serir deserts are covered with pebbles and gravel left behind after fine sand is blown away by wind deflation.",
        "Hamada deserts consist of bare, wind-scoured bedrock surfaces cleared entirely of sand deposits.",
        "Badlands feature deeply eroded terrains characterized by intricate networks of gullies, ravines, and sharp ridges."
      ],
